Zode
====

Zode is a fork of Zed (https://github.com/zed-industries/zed), the code
editor built by Zed Industries, Inc. and its contributors.

This fork removes Zed's authentication, cloud, in-editor AI, collaboration,
edit-prediction, telemetry, and crash-reporting subsystems, in order to
produce an independent editor that collects no usage data. It adds an optional
account used solely to sync the user's own settings, keymap and installed-
extension list, encrypted on their machine with a key the server never
receives; it is off unless the user signs in. Some AI settings-schema and
URL-builder code remains in the tree with no remaining call sites; no model
call is made from it. See legal/privacy-policy.md for the full statement of
what leaves the machine, including the one request Zode makes automatically.
